    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Looking at the BT data there isn&#39;t a model I could explicitly specify for this case.</div><div>The main question is whether I can model explanatory variables at the same time as the response variables. In my fake example above I used <span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\">bf_hatchdate &lt;- bf(</span><span></span><span>hatchdate ~ foo + bar)</span>  and then included that in bf_back. Would that syntax work? </div></div>"
    ],
