     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Looking at the BT data there isn&#39;t a model I could explicitly specify for this case.</div><div>The main question is whether I can model explanatory variables at the same time as the response variables. In my fake example above I used <span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\">bf_hatchdate &lt;- bf(</span><span></span><span>hatchdate ~ foo + bar)</span>  and then included that in bf_back. Would that syntax work? <br><br>On Saturday, December 16, 2017 at 10:11:53 PM UTC+1, Paul Buerkner wrote:</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\">Can you write down explictely what model you want to specify? Maybe it is already possible with brms 2.0</div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">Am 16.12.2017 21:42 schrieb &quot;Simon Fraval&quot; &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">simon...@gmail.com</a>&gt;:<br type=\"attribution\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>It&#39;s great to see the release of version 2.0 - nice work Paul!</div><div><br></div><div>Multivariate models are working very nicely. I like the flexibility of being able to specify simpler models with multiple response variables from different families, or to get more detailed by specifying different formulas. </div><div>One question while my computer is tied up sampling: can we specify network models with this syntax? For example, can we model something like this below?</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre-wrap;margin:5px 0px 10px;padding:10px;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:18px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px\"><code style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span></span><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\">bf_hatchdate &lt;- bf(<span></span><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\">hatchdate ~ foo + bar)</span></span></code></pre><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre-wrap;margin:5px 0px 10px;padding:10px;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:18px;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px\"><code style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\"></span>bf_tarsus &lt;-<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-weight:bold\">bf</span>(tarsus <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>sex <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>p<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>fosternest) <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>q<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>dam))\r\nbf_back &lt;-<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-weight:bold\">bf</span>(back <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>bf_hatchdate <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>p<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>fosternest) <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>q<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">|</span>dam))\r\nfit &lt;-<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-weight:bold\">brm</span>(bf_tarsus <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> </span>bf_back, <span style=\"color:rgb(144,32,0)\">data =</span> BTdata, <span style=\"color:rgb(144,32,0)\">chains =</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(144,32,0)\">cores =</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">2</span>)</code></pre></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;brms-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">brms-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">brms-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/87ade66d-6ddf-49d3-8352-35634b9a1260%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/87ade66d-6ddf-49d3-8352-35634b9a1260%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451636136000&amp;usg=AOvVaw349vp1yrd6WMQsEMJm-swt\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/87ade66d-6ddf-49d3-8352-35634b9a1260%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://